(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The full C API's layouts (queue 269; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 269\"; 262's DECISION (a), the user"] [4 1 "// 2026-11-10, and 268's DECISION (a), 2026-11-11). Without Py_LIMITED_API, CPython 3.14.10's Include/ reads objects in"] [5 1 "// place: Py_TYPE(o)->tp_flags (PyTuple_Check and the other subclass checks), PyList_Type.tp_new, PyTuple_GET_ITEM's"] [6 1 "// ob_item, PyList_GET_ITEM's ob_item array, PyBytes_AS_STRING's ob_sval, PyFloat_AS_DOUBLE's ob_fval. So:"] [7 1 "//"] [8 1 "//   - a type's handle is a PyTypeObject (PyHeapTypeObject's 936 bytes, or the world's static struct of a type"] [9 1 "//     Include/ names) filled as CPython's: tp_name, the sizes, tp_flags, tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, and its"] [10 1 "//     function slots (a type made from a spec its C functions, a pyi type the natives of the generic protocol);"] [11 1 "//   - a tuple's, list's, bytes' and float's handle is a mirror: the object's CPython layout in the world's memory,"] [12 1 "//     made when C first sees the object and kept in step with the pyi value at the C boundary, both ways (as PyPy's"] [13 1 "//     cpyext does): from Go to C before the world is called and when a native returns (the objects it touched), from"] [14 1 "//     C to Go when the world returns and when a native receives a mirrored object (its first use in the native). A"] [15 1 "//     container's mirror holds references to its items' handles, as CPython's container holds its items: a slot C"] [16 1 "//     writes (PyTuple_SET_ITEM, PyList_SET_ITEM) steals the reference C gave, a slot Go changes holds a new one and"] [17 1 "//     gives the old one back, and a mirror released gives its items back."] [18 1 "//"] [19 1 "// Layouts from Include/cpython/{object,tupleobject,listobject,bytesobject,floatobject}.h (CPython 3.14.10, LP64; the"] [20 1 "// PSF's license, LICENSE.md); the slots' offsets are Objects/typeslots.inc's."] [36 1 "// PyTypeObject's and PyHeapTypeObject's fields (offsets, LP64)"] [38 28 "// sizeof(PyHeapTypeObject)"] [70 1 "// slotOffsets is Objects/typeslots.inc (slot id -> the sub-struct's field offset, -1 for none, and the type's field"] [71 1 "// offset), from CPython 3.14.10's headers by gcc (offsetof, LP64)."] [81 1 "// the heap type's own sub-structs (PyHeapTypeObject's as_async, as_number, ...), by the type's field that points"] [82 1 "// at one"] [86 1 "// builtinTpFlags are CPython 3.14.10's tp_flags of the types Include/ names (type.__flags__, python3 3.14.10)."] [102 1 "// typeFlags is t's tp_flags as a C reader sees them: CPython's own for the types Include/ names, a type's made from a"] [103 1 "// spec or by PyType_Ready its own, else the subclass bits, BASETYPE and HEAPTYPE pyi knows, READY, the version tag,"] [104 1 "// IMMUTABLETYPE for a static type, and HAVE_GC for a heap type."] [107 52 "// inherit_special: the base's fast-subclass bits"] [121 1 "// cTpName is tp_name: a C type's own, a heap class's __name__, a static type's module-qualified name outside builtins."] [132 1 "// genericSlots are the natives a pyi type's function slots point at (the generic protocol's functions of the same"] [133 1 "// signature), by slot id: C calling Py_TYPE(o)->tp_repr(o) calls PyObject_Repr."] [139 1 "// fillTypeObject writes t's PyTypeObject at a (its handle: the head is written by the caller; the fields of a"] [140 1 "// PyHeapTypeObject's size, or of a static struct's)."] [170 2 "// the function slots: a C type's own (its spec's or PyType_Ready's, inherited), else the generic natives"] [176 57 "// tp_doc: the spec's copy (queue 270b)"] [178 3 "// ht_name, ht_qualname (queue 270b: test_type_from_ephemeral_spec reads them)"] [219 1 "// storeSlot writes the function fn into the slot id of the type object at a (its sub-struct's field when the type"] [220 1 "// has that sub-struct)."] [233 1 "// loadSlot reads the slot id of the type object at a (0: none, or no sub-struct)."] [246 1 "// ---- mirrors ----"] [248 1 "// mirror is the CPython layout of a tuple, list, bytes, float, int or str in the world's memory, a handle's."] [250 17 "// 't' tuple, 'l' list, 'b' bytes, 'f' float, 'i' int, 'u' str"] [251 17 "// the pyi object (a subclass's instance too: its built-in part is mirrored)"] [252 17 "// a tuple's or list's slots as last synchronized"] [253 17 "// a bytes' contents as last synchronized"] [254 17 "// the synchronization epoch of the last copy from C"] [255 2 "// a str's (queue 270, capi_unicode.go): its kind, ASCII flag and characters' address; a str PyUnicode_New made"] [256 2 "// (fresh) keeps a copy of its characters to see what C writes"] [265 2 "// held are the references mirrors hold on their items' handles because Go put the item there (a reference C"] [266 2 "// wrote into a slot is C's own): \"C holds the only reference\" (a brand-new object) is a count less these of 1"] [269 28 "// the mirrors a native (or a closure) used: synchronized to C when it returns"] [273 1 "// mirrorKind is the layout o's handle mirrors (0: a proxy's head only) and the bytes it needs."] [287 19 "// PyByteArrayObject (queue 270: PyByteArray_AS_STRING, GET_SIZE)"] [309 1 "// longDigits are an int's absolute value in CPython's 30-bit digits, least significant first (none for 0)."] [321 1 "// writeLong writes an int's PyLongObject fields at a (Include/cpython/longintrepr.h, 3.14: lv_tag is the digits'"] [322 1 "// count shifted by 3 with the sign in the low bits, 0 positive, 1 zero, 2 negative; then the digits)."] [340 1 "// asFloatValue is a float's (or a float subclass's instance's) value."] [354 1 "// newMirror writes o's layout at a (its handle, the head written) and records the mirror."] [373 31 "// ob_shash: -1, not computed"] [380 31 "// ob_hash: -1, not computed"] [389 1 "// syncToC writes the pyi value's state into its mirror (the slots Go changed: a new reference to the new item, the"] [390 1 "// old one's given back)."] [395 3 "// a bytearray: ob_size, ob_alloc, ob_bytes, ob_start (Include/cpython/bytearrayobject.h); its storage a block of"] [396 3 "// the world's, made again when it grows"] [478 1 "// syncFromC copies what C wrote into its mirror to the pyi value (the slots C changed; a NULL slot is a nil item, as"] [479 1 "// CPython's NULL until C fills it), and does so for the mirrors its items name, once an epoch."] [508 3 "// C's slots as last synchronized: C changed nothing, so Go's value stands (Python code a native ran may have"] [509 3 "// resized the list since: gh-72054's __index__ popping from it, test_slice's getindicesex_seq), written to C"] [510 3 "// when the native that uses it returns"] [542 10 "// resized from C: not provided (PyByteArray_Resize is a native)"] [565 1 "// holdRef and unholdRef are a mirror's reference to an item Go put in it, and its giving back."] [585 1 "// cOnly reports whether C holds the only reference to the handle h (its count, less the mirrors' own, is 1)."] [588 1 "// rawObj is the object a handle names without synchronizing it (nil for NULL)."] [597 1 "// freeMirror releases a mirror's own memory and its items' references (its handle released)."] [617 1 "// syncAllToC writes every mirror's pyi state into C (before the world is called: Python code may have changed any)."] [624 1 "// syncAllFromC copies every mirror's C state to its pyi value (when the world returns to Python)."] [632 1 "// nativeEnter and nativeLeave bracket a native's (or a closure's) run: what C wrote is copied to Go on the first use"] [633 1 "// of a mirrored object in it (fromHandle), and the mirrors it used are written back to C when it returns."] [654 1 "// touch marks a mirrored handle as used by the running native."] [663 1 "// ---- C types over a built-in base (268's DECISION (a), the user 2026-11-11) ----"] [665 1 "// born is a C type's instance over a built-in base (a type a spec or PyType_Ready made, deriving from list, tuple,"] [666 1 "// bytes or float): its memory is the world's, tp_bas