fills, then PyType_Ready's)."] [834 3 "// a type object (a C metaclass's too, queue 270b: its basicsize, the C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject)"] [861 1 "// rawTypes are the type objects C allocated through type's tp_alloc, not ready yet."] [864 1 "// bornDealloc is a built-in base's tp_dealloc on a C instance's memory (list_dealloc, tupledealloc ...): its items'"] [865 1 "// references given back as CPython's do, read from its memory, the list's array and the memory freed."] [887 1 "// ---- PyType_Ready for a type object of C's memory (a static PyTypeObject, or one C filled after type's tp_alloc) ----"] [889 1 "// typeReady is PyType_Ready (Objects/typeobject.c, type_ready) of the type object at a: a pyi type made from its"] [890 1 "// fields (NewExtType), its slots the C functions it names and those it inherits, its handle a; the fields"] [891 1 "// PyType_Ready fills written back (tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, the inherited slots, Py_TPFLAGS_READY)."] [917 2 "// the base and the bases"] [980 39 "// type_ready_set_new: a static type over object without tp_new"] [982 2 "// inherit_slots: a C base's, else the generic natives of a pyi base"] [996 3 "// inherit_slots (queue 270b): tp_vectorcall_offset, Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_VECTORCALL when tp_call is inherited (a"] [997 3 "// static type is immutable), Py_TPFLAGS_METHOD_DESCRIPTOR when tp_descr_get is"] [1011 14 "// pyi's own (the base's slots) unless C's"] [1020 2 "// the type's own"] [1033 28 "// the base's own __new__ (tp_alloc's allocation through allocObj)"] [1041 2 "// the handle is the C memory"] [1060 2 "// what PyType_Ready writes back"] [1094 2 "// a pyi base's protocol slots C reads in place (Py_TYPE(o)->tp_free, tp_alloc ...)"] [1105 1 "// builtinBaseOf is the nearest type of t's MRO that is neither a C type nor a heap class (the built-in whose"] [1106 1 "// tp_new and tp_init a C type's instance inherits)."] [1116 1 "// callTupleDict calls f with a C call's positional tuple and keywords' dict (NULL: none) after the leading arguments."] [1143 1 "// mirrorTable: the natives of the full API's layouts (queue 269)."] [1170 2 "// tp_new of a pyi type: a C type's instance over a built-in base allocated (bornNew), else the built-in's __new__"] [1219 2 "// tp_dealloc of a pyi type: a C instance's built-in part given back and its memory freed (a pyi object's own"] [1220 2 "// memory is Go's: nothing)"] [1238 2 "// _PyTuple_Resize (Objects/tupleobject.c): *p a tuple only C holds, made newsize long (a new tuple: pyi's are"] [1239 2 "// Go's), the items past the end given back, the new ones NULL"] [1274 2 "// PyErr_NewException (Python/errors.c): a class NAME's last part, of base (Exception by default; a tuple of bases"] [1275 2 "// too) and dict, its __module__ NAME's first part"] [1306 2 "// PyObject_CallFunction, PyObject_CallMethod (Objects/call.c): the arguments Py_BuildValue's format makes, a tuple"] [1307 2 "// its items"] [1394 2 "// _PyObject_GC_New (Python/gc.c; the limited API's PyObject_GC_New before 3.8, xxlimited_35's, py-eval-1122): _PyObject_New's"] [1395 2 "// (pyi's collector tracks the object; PyObject_GC_Track and PyObject_GC_Del as before)"] [1418 2 "// PyWeakref_GetRef, PyWeakref_IsDead (Objects/weakrefobject.c) over pyi's references and proxies (PyWeakref_Check:"] [1419 2 "// a ref, a proxy or a callable proxy); the referent, or nil when it is dead"] [1493 21 "// big-endian"] [1511 2 "// PyCFunction_Call (Objects/methodobject.c, the stable ABI's): PyObject_Call"] [1513 2 "// _PyArg_ParseStack (Python/getargs.c): PyArg_ParseTuple's format over a vectorcall's stack (clinic's parsers)"] [1525 2 "// _PyBytes_Resize (Objects/bytesobject.c): *p a bytes only C holds, made newsize long (a new bytes: pyi's value"] [1526 2 "// is Go's; its contents copied from the mirror, which C may have written), NULL and the error on failure"] [1553 1 "// ---- instancemethod (Objects/classobject.c's PyInstanceMethod_Type; queue 269: _testcapi names it) ----"] [1557 1 "// instance